<article class="env-definition" id="0B8H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B8H">Definition <span data-tag="0B8H">15.119.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. An $R$-module $M$ is <em>invertible</em> if the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Mod}_ R \longrightarrow \text{Mod}_ R,\quad N \longmapsto M \otimes _ R N  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. An invertible $R$-module is said to be <em>trivial</em> if it is isomorphic to $R$ as an $R$-module. </p>
</article>